# File commands

File commands run locally and do not start the daemon.

- meno read FILE [START END] [--hash]
- meno edit FILE OLD NEW
- meno edit FILE --json [--expect-hash HASH] (reads edits from stdin)
- meno write FILE [--overwrite] (reads content from stdin)
- meno search PATTERN [DIR] [--regex] [--glob G] [--limit N]

Use '-' as a file path to read stdin where the command accepts input.
